# Implementation nodes' git worktrees, one per claimed node.
# Inside the repository so the human's review sees them; ignored so they are not
# committed. See .scratch/graph-workflow/map-manager-only.md, "Landing an
# implementation node's work".
.worktrees/

# The git worktrees the agent harness creates for implementation workers, one per
# claimed node. Ignored so those worktrees are never committed. The entry above is
# the path the landing policy used when the manager created worktrees by hand.
# See .scratch/graph-workflow/map-manager-only.md, "How the worktree is made".
.claude/worktrees/

# The current path. It holds one git worktree per claimed implementation node,
# created with plain `git worktree add` rather than by the harness, and placed
# inside the repository so that a review can see the diff. Ignored so those
# worktrees are never committed. The two entries above are the paths used by the
# earlier routes.
# See .scratch/graph-workflow/map-manager-only.md, "How the worktree is made".
.scratch/graph-workflow/worktrees/
